3.2 Brownian Bridge Diffusion Models
A Brownian Bridge Diffusion Model (BBDM) [19] is an image-to-image translation framework based on a stochastic Brownian Bridge process. Unlike DDPM that conclude at Gaussian noise xT ∼ N (0, I), BBDM assumes that both endpoints of the diffusion process as fixed data points from an arbitrary joint distribution, i.e. (xT , x0) ∼ qdata(X , Y). The BBDM directly learns image-to-image translation q(x0|xT ) with boundary distribution qdata(x0, xT ) independent of any conditional process, that enhances the fidelity and diversity of the generated samples. The forward process of the Brownian Bridge forms a bridge between two fixed endpoints at t = 0 and T :
