4 Limitations
Our approach utilizes the Brownian Bridge diffusion process in latent space [34] to connect control and image latents effectively. However, the pre-trained VAE Encoder that focuses on image representation limits its ability to process control signals accurately, especially when differentiating semantically diverse elements (such as background and face in mask), focusing more on color distance rather than semantic discrepancies. To mitigate this, prior studies [57, 60] have introduced additional control guiders. Yet, integrating these with the Brownian Bridge model, characterized by its reliance on two fixed endpoints, complicates the direct integration of such solutions.


